---
import { tagStyles } from 'ui/base/tag/tag.styles';

const STACK_CAPTION_ID = 'meetmedia-stack';
const STACK = ['HTML', 'CSS', 'Sass', 'JavaScript', 'jQuery', 'PHP'];
---

<div class="space-y-element">
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <h3 class="text-2xl">Meetmedia</h3>
    <p class="text-text-secondary">Junior Frontend Developer &middot; Dec 2019 &ndash; Aug 2020 &middot; Remote</p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The role before the framework &mdash; layout, CSS and browser debugging built by hand, from Photoshop designs, with
    nothing generating the markup.
  </p>

  <ul class="space-y-2">
    <li>
      The complete visual layer of bezuzyteczna.pl, a well-known Polish content portal &mdash; cut from PSD and wired to
      the site&rsquo;s logic and API. Still running unchanged in production six years later.
    </li>
    <li>
      Client sites built and maintained end to end in semantic HTML, Sass and JavaScript &mdash; reported symptom
      reproduced in the browser, traced to root cause, fixed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="space-y-2">
    <p id={STACK_CAPTION_ID} class="text-text-secondary">Stack at the time</p>
    <ul aria-labelledby={STACK_CAPTION_ID} class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {STACK.map((item) => <li class={tagStyles}>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
